<title>USA: U.S. aluminum center shipments rise year to date.</title>
<headline>U.S. aluminum center shipments rise year to date.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Service center shipments of aluminum mill products for the two months ended February 1997 were 6.7 percent above shipments for the same period in 1996, the National Assocation of Aluminum Distributors reported.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three-month moving average index, shipments in February rose to 140.9 points from 139.4 points in January and 138.4 points in December.</p>
<p>Inventory climbed to 124.9 points in February from 122.8 points in January, still equal to 2.8 months of inventory.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
